{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917469472},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to answer a data question about farmers markets per 100,000 residents in the U.S. I have two data sources:\n1. https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv (farmers markets by state)\n2. https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv (census/population data)\n\nFollowing the xorq analyst instructions, I should:\n1. First check `xorq_semantic_models` to see if there's already a reviewed measure for this\n2. Check `xorq_catalog_list_aliases` to see if these datasets are already in the catalog\n3. If not, I'll need to ingest them\n4. Create a derived metric (farmers markets per 100,000 residents)\n5. Use `xorq_select` to get the value\n6. Use `xorq_verify` to verify the value with an obligation\n\nThe task says to use tools to do any math necessary - I should compose a metric in the catalog rather than computing it myself.\n\nLet me start by checking the catalog for existing aliases and semantic models.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you find the number of farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking the xorq catalog for any existing data."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01XwoHrBTwEWdXFUUQ76wp4Q","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01GieRNzLsAbBDT